e_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Blackstone Secured Lending Fund is business development company and a Delaware statutory trust formed on March 26, 2018, and structured as an externally managed, non-diversified closed-end investment Fund. On October 26, 2018, the fund elected to be regulated as a business development company (\u0093BDC\u0094) under the Investment Company Act of 1940, as amended (the \u00931940 Act\u0094). In addition, the Fund elected to be treated for U.S. federal income tax purposes, as a regulated investment company (\u0093RIC\u0094), as defined under Subchapter M of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended (the \u0093Code\u0094). The fund also intends to continue to comply with the requirements prescribed by the Code in order to maintain tax treatment as a RIC. The fund's investment objectives are to generate current income and, to a lesser extent, long-term capital appreciation. The Fund seeks to achieve its investment objective primarily through originated loans, equity and other securities, including syndicated loans, of private U.S. companies, specifically small and middle market companies, typically in the form of first lien senior secured and unitranche loans (including first out/last out loans), and to a lesser extent, second lien, third lien, unsecured and subordinated loans and other debt and equity securities.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brad  Marshall | Global Head of Private Credit Strategies, Chairman & CEO | Age 53","financial_summary":["Blackstone Secured Lending Fund is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.6B market cap.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.0% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 53% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Contrast: Jefferies Financial Group (NYSE:JEF) versus Blackstone Secured Lending Fund (NYSE:BXSL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/head-to-head-contrast-jefferies-financial-group-nysejef-versus-blackstone-secured-lending-fund-nysebxsl.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977139.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Blackstone Lending (BXSL) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/blackstone-lending-bxsl-q3-2026-190124000.html","date":"2026-11-04",